definition.doc:
NXlaser_pump_probe as written at HZDR's DRACO petawatt laser: shot-based laser-
plasma experiments, one shot authority issuing every shot number, an electronic
logbook (LabFrog, being brought into use at DRACO) that records each shot's
status, and campaigns compared with PIConGPU simulations. Uses the modules:
high-intensity, simulation, provenance. Not used at this site:
/ENTRY/events/sub_index; /ENTRY/events/pump_state;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/source_probe/mode;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/source_probe/number_of_bunches;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/source_probe/bunch_distance;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/source_probe/bunch_length;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/synchronization/locked;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/synchronization/reference_frequency;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/synchronization/frequency_ratio; /ENTRY/SAMPLE/identifier.
Still to confirm at this site: /ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/source_pump/pulse_shape;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_pump/incident_polarization_stokes;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_pump/fluence;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_probe/pulse_delay_set;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/synchronization/time_zero;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/synchronization/timing_jitter;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/synchronization/arrival_time_correction;
/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/DETECTOR/trigger_delay_time_set. Items marked SITE are this
site's own and are not proposed for the core. Generated by make_site.py from
sites/hzdr_draco.marks.yaml; edit that file, not this one.
